window.docContents[83].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.AEAD.Aes256/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___AEAD___Aes256":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/AEAD › Aes256.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof and symbolic proof 8 headline theorems depend on it 150 of 216 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (27)abbrev Stateabbrev Worddef sboxTabledef invSboxTabledef sboxdef invSboxdef xtimedef gfMuldef subBytesdef invSubBytesdef shiftRowsdef invShiftRowsdef mixColumndef mixColumnsdef invMixColumndef invMixColumnsdef addRoundKeydef rotWorddef subWorddef xorWorddef rcondef expandKey256def roundKeydef aes256Cipherdef aes256InvCipherdef aes256Encdef aes256Dec\n\nFIPS 197 AES-256 Block Cipher SpecificationTrusted: definitions used by the statement. Direct transcription of NIST FIPS 197 for AES-256 (Nk = 8, Nb = 4, Nr = 14), bridging FIPS 197 column-major 16-byte states (aes256Cipher, aes256InvCipher) to the repository's little-endian CBC.AesKey / CBC.Block representation (aes256Enc, aes256Dec). See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.\n\n\n\nSection 1: Pure FIPS 197 AES-256 Specification\n\nabbrev StateL35–37 ↗#Column-major 16-byte AES state: row r, column c (0 ≤ r, c < 4) sits at s[r + 4 * c] (FIPS 197 §3.4, Eq. 3.3).\n\nabbrev WordL39–40 ↗#A 4-byte key-schedule column word (FIPS 197 §3.2).\n\ndef sboxTableL42–60 ↗#Forward AES S-box 16×16 lookup table indexed by high/low nibble (FIPS 197 §5.1.1, Figure 7).\n\ndef invSboxTableL62–80 ↗#Inverse AES S-box 16×16 lookup table indexed by high/low nibble (FIPS 197 §5.3.2, Figure 14).\n\ndef sboxL82–83 ↗#Single-byte S-box substitution SBox(b) (FIPS 197 §5.1.1).\n\ndef invSboxL85–86 ↗#Single-byte inverse S-box substitution InvSBox(b) (FIPS 197 §5.3.2).\n\ndef xtimeL88–91 ↗#Multiplication by $x$ ({02}) in $\\mathrm{GF}(2^8) = \\mathbb{F}_2[x]/(x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1)$ (FIPS 197 §4.2.1).\n\ndef gfMulL93–96 ↗#Multiplication in $\\mathrm{GF}(2^8)$ via repeated xtime (FIPS 197 §4.2.1).\n\ndef subBytesL98–99 ↗#SubBytes state transformation (FIPS 197 §5.1.1).\n\ndef invSubBytesL101–102 ↗#InvSubBytes state transformation (FIPS 197 §5.3.2).\n\ndef shiftRowsL104–110 ↗#ShiftRows state transformation: row r shifts cyclically left by r columns (s'[r, c] = s[r, (c + r) mod 4], FIPS 197 §5.1.2).\n\ndef invShiftRowsL112–118 ↗#InvShiftRows state transformation: row r shifts cyclically right by r columns (s'[r, c] = s[r, (c - r) mod 4], FIPS 197 §5.3.1).\n\ndef mixColumnL120–125 ↗#Mix one 4-byte state column (FIPS 197 §5.1.3, Eq. 5.6).\n\ndef mixColumnsL127–131 ↗#MixColumns state transformation across all four columns (FIPS 197 §5.1.3).\n\ndef invMixColumnL133–138 ↗#Inverse-mix one 4-byte state column (FIPS 197 §5.3.3, Eq. 5.10).\n\ndef invMixColumnsL140–144 ↗#InvMixColumns state transformation across all four columns (FIPS 197 §5.3.3).\n\ndef addRoundKeyL146–148 ↗#AddRoundKey state transformation (FIPS 197 §5.1.4).\n\ndef rotWordL150–152 ↗#Cyclic 1-byte left word rotation [a₀, a₁, a₂, a₃] ↦ [a₁, a₂, a₃, a₀] (FIPS 197 §5.2).\n\ndef subWordL154–155 ↗#Bytewise S-box substitution on a 4-byte word (FIPS 197 §5.2).\n\ndef xorWordL157–159 ↗#Bytewise XOR of two 4-byte words.\n\ndef rconL161–163 ↗#Round-constant leading bytes Rcon[1..7] for AES-256 (Nk = 8, FIPS 197 §5.2 Table 5).\n\ndef expandKey256L165–180 ↗#AES-256 key expansion (Nk = 8, Nb = 4, Nr = 14 → 60 words; FIPS 197 §5.2, Algorithm 2).\n\ndef roundKeyL182–184 ↗#Extract 16-byte round key r (0 ≤ r ≤ 14) from the 60-word key schedule w[4r .. 4r+3].\n\ndef aes256CipherL186–192 ↗#FIPS 197 §5.1 Algorithm 1 (Cipher for AES-256, Nr = 14).\n\ndef aes256InvCipherL194–200 ↗#FIPS 197 §5.3 Algorithm 3 (InvCipher for AES-256, Nr = 14).\n\nSection 2: Little-Endian CBC.AesKey / CBC.Block Byte-Order Glue\n\ndef aes256EncL205–208 ↗#AES-256 single-block encryption (CBC.AesKey → CBC.Block → CBC.Block) under the repository's little-endian byte encoding (HMAC.keyToBytes32, CBC.blockToBytesLE, CBC.bytesToBlock).\n\ndef aes256DecL210–213 ↗#AES-256 single-block decryption (CBC.AesKey → CBC.Block → CBC.Block) under the repository's little-endian byte encoding (HMAC.keyToBytes32, CBC.blockToBytesLE, CBC.bytesToBlock).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/AEAD/Aes256.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.CryptoGames.AEAD.Aes256/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___CryptoGames___AEAD___Aes256"}});